<title>RUSSIA: AGROKHLEB-Russia '97 spring wheat sowing up on '96.</title>
<headline>AGROKHLEB-Russia '97 spring wheat sowing up on '96.</headline>
<text>
<p>The following is a direct contribution from SovEcon Ltd, an independent research organisation specialising in agricultural production and trade in the former Soviet Union.</p>
<p>RUSSIA: SPRING WHEAT SOWINGS IN 1997 WELL AHEAD OF 1996 LEVELS</p>
<p>MOSCOW, May 12 - Russia's spring wheat sowing campaign had started in all Russian regions by the end of April, including the major wheat-producing areas of the Urals and Western and Eastern Siberia.</p>
<p>Assuming normal development of spring wheat sowing from now on, SovEcon expects Russia's total spring wheat area to reach or even slightly exceed last year's record level of 16.4 million hectares.</p>
<p>The early pick-up in sowing rates reflects favourable weather conditions in most grain producing regions, particularly in Western and Eastern Siberia.</p>
<p>It should also reduce the risk of crop losses because of adverse weather conditions during harvesting in Siberia.</p>
